{"id":"a3","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":3,"of":19,"title":"One and many","titleHe":"יָחִיד וְרַבִּים","goal":"Form plurals, and recognise the irregular ones you'll use daily.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"Masculine nouns take ־ִים, feminine nouns take ־וֹת. The vowels inside the word usually shorten when the ending is added."},{"type":"table","caption":"Regular plurals","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["סֵפֶר — book","סְפָרִים"],["יֶלֶד — boy","יְלָדִים"],["מוֹרָה — teacher (f.)","מוֹרוֹת"],["מִשְׁפָּחָה — family","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת"]]},{"type":"tip","body":"The ending does not always match the gender. שֻׁלְחָן is masculine but pluralises שֻׁלְחָנוֹת; שָׁנָה is feminine but goes שָׁנִים. The gender doesn't change — only the ending is irregular."},{"type":"table","caption":"The irregulars worth memorising","head":["singular","plural"],"rows":[["אִישׁ — man","אֲנָשִׁים"],["אִשָּׁה — woman","נָשִׁים"],["בַּיִת — house","בָּתִּים"],["בֵּן — son","בָּנִים"],["בַּת — daughter","בָּנוֹת"],["שָׁנָה — year","שָׁנִים"]]}],"vocab":[{"he":"אִישׁ","en":"man","translit":"ish"},{"he":"אִשָּׁה","en":"woman","translit":"isha"},{"he":"אֲנָשִׁים","en":"people, men","translit":"anashim"},{"he":"נָשִׁים","en":"women","translit":"nashim"},{"he":"בָּתִּים","en":"houses","translit":"batim"},{"he":"סְפָרִים","en":"books","translit":"sfarim"},{"he":"יְלָדִים","en":"children","translit":"yeladim"},{"he":"שָׁנָה","en":"year","translit":"shana"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["at most","man","grandfather","late"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִישׁ","translit":"ish"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["butterfly","woman","onion","don't (with the future)"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אִשָּׁה","translit":"isha"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["while","people, men","morals, rebuke","open"],"correct":1,"prompt":"אֲנָשִׁים","translit":"anashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["first","ordinary, used to","women","feeling"],"correct":2,"prompt":"נָשִׁים","translit":"nashim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["houses","wakes up","maybe","stomach, belly"],"correct":0,"prompt":"בָּתִּים","translit":"batim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["grandson","cheap","question","books"],"correct":3,"prompt":"סְפָרִים","translit":"sfarim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["children","matter, interest","butterfly","a letter of the alphabet"],"correct":0,"prompt":"יְלָדִים","translit":"yeladim"},{"type":"choice","q":"What's the plural of אִשָּׁה?","options":["נָשִׁים","אִשּׁוֹת","אֲנָשִׁים","אִשִּׁים"],"correct":0,"why":"אִשָּׁה → נָשִׁים is irregular; אֲנָשִׁים is the plural of אִישׁ, man."},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — house?","options":["אֲנָשִׁים","בָּנִים","נָשִׁים","בָּתִּים"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"Regular plurals — teacher (f.)?","options":["סְפָרִים","יְלָדִים","מוֹרוֹת","מִשְׁפָּחוֹת"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"match","pairs":[["אִישׁ","man"],["אִשָּׁה","woman"],["אֲנָשִׁים","people, men"],["נָשִׁים","women"],["בָּתִּים","houses"]]},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — daughter?","options":["אֲנָשִׁים","נָשִׁים","בָּתִּים","בָּנוֹת"],"correct":3,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"The irregulars worth memorising — year?","options":["נָשִׁים","שָׁנִים","בָּתִּים","אֲנָשִׁים"],"correct":1,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “year”?","options":["שָׁנָה","מִתְעוֹרֵר","כְּאֵב","נֶפֶשׁ"],"correct":0,"he":true},{"type":"choice","q":"How do you say “children”?","options":["רוֹעֵשׁ","סוֹלְלָה","יְלָדִים","שָׁלֵם"],"correct":2,"he":true},{"type":"type","q":"Write “woman” in Hebrew","answer":"אִשָּׁה","hint":"isha"}]}